    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "Hello.\r\n\r\nA lot of LSPs will include snippets when a function is completed.\r\nNeovim has a built in method for handling these but it requires you also use its built in LSP completion feature as well.\r\n\r\nDoes or will mini.completion support snippet expansion? What I mean by this is when a function is being completed hitting <Tab> will move you to each argument where you can fill in the variables you want to include in the final function call syntax.",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Hello.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">A lot of LSPs will include snippets when a function is completed.<br>\nNeovim has a built in method for handling these but it requires you also use its built in LSP completion feature as well.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Does or will mini.completion support snippet expansion? What I mean by this is when a function is being completed hitting  will move you to each argument where you can fill in the variables you want to include in the final function call syntax.</p>",
    "bodyText": "Hello.\nA lot of LSPs will include snippets when a function is completed.\nNeovim has a built in method for handling these but it requires you also use its built in LSP completion feature as well.\nDoes or will mini.completion support snippet expansion? What I mean by this is when a function is being completed hitting  will move you to each argument where you can fill in the variables you want to include in the final function call syntax.",
